  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance sanitaire anticipatoire des populations affect&#xe9;es par la s&#xe8;cheresse</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main aim of this $549,987 WHO project is to mitigate the health-related consequences of drought in Niger through early detection, vaccination and access to emergency health care. To that end, WHO will reinforce 3 rapid response teams, vaccinate 6,400 children against measles, and deliver 6,366 emergency health kits to four health centers in the target regions. In total, WHO expects to assist 30,625 people, including 9,684 women and 5,935 girls. Among those targeted WHO expects to 1,225 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
